  "details": "It's not a secret, that's a lot of ppl using VPN for various reasons, most common is own privacy/security and government censorship bypass.\nHowever, VPN is not only way to do that, another popular way is to use proxy servers, especially SOCKS5, which can handle packets of almost all common networking protocols.\nSOCKS5 is simplier to setup, as it does not requires tunnels, in general does not requires special software, or any support or special conditions by OS. (As example, SOCKS5 may be opened over SSH by single command line, regardless OS)\nHowever, without support from the app or without using special software, you can not use it. A lot of popular networking software such as torrents and browsers, supports SOCKS5, making it easy to use. And that's important: while VPN is system wide, SOCKS5 can be used only if necessary in specific apps. \nUnfortunately, VRChat does not supports SOCKS5 explicitly. It's possible to warp VRChat into SOCKS5 using special software, but, I believe, as VRChat has http/https/websocket-based internals it's technically should not be that hard to implement, most web networking libararies supports it out of the box.\nA few more words about government censorship. In Russia, some of CloudFlare IPs and Amazon ( https://reestr.rublacklist.net/search/?q=amazonaws.com ) servers are banned, VRChat uses these services, so it's a common thing in russian community when previews, avatars and worlds randomly stops loading. In VRChat official Discord in #russian, and in community servers we can see how people often complaining about loading errors and discuss VPN services. Same applies to (continental) China - I have some friends and they also complaining about that. Alongside VPN, SOCKS5 is popular with advanced users, as they can quickly switch app to SOCKS5 or use it only for services having issues (for exmple, PAC-scripts in Russia, such as https://antizapret.prostovpn.org/proxy.pac ).\nAlso, Using apps like VRChat does not always against rules at workplaces (mine allows :D), but corporative networks often uses SOCKS5 to proivde access from LAN to WAN (especially in small organizations where complex networking setup is not necessary), and there is hard to run VRChat in these conditions.\nI hope, devs can provide something like command line arguments to allow connect VRChat using given SOCKS5.",
